00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:32,267
Let's try it again.

520
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:34,200
I take the quarter and rub it

521
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,667
and it's gone.

522
00:20:35,667 --> 00:20:36,833
- Hey, cool.

523
00:20:36,833 --> 00:20:38,100
- Okay, can I go now?

524
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,133
- Now, you must walk
us on the ceiling.

525
00:20:40,133 --> 00:20:41,600
- No, Crow, in character.

526
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,167
You must walk us on
the ceiling, human.

527
00:20:44,167 --> 00:20:46,333
- You guys, you guys
know you're getting

528
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:47,400
way too big for that.

529
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,600
I can't walk you on the ceiling.

530
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:49,967
What else you want me to do?

531
00:20:51,233 --> 00:20:53,533
- You must create a
severe weather condition

532
00:20:53,533 --> 00:20:54,800
inside the satellite.

533
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,633
- Yeah.

534
00:20:55,633 --> 00:20:56,867
- Like what?

535
00:20:56,867 --> 00:20:58,133
- You know, the
Chinese snow trick.

536
00:20:58,133 --> 00:20:59,367
- I can't do snow
storm in China.

537
00:20:59,367 --> 00:21:00,967
It's in the shop, I'd
have to go get it.

538
00:21:00,967 --> 00:21:02,500
What can I do that's real quick?

539
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:03,967
- Do goofus face for us.

540
00:21:03,967 --> 00:21:06,267
- Yeah, crazy duck face.

541
00:21:06,267 --> 00:21:07,100
- Okay.

542
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,033
I'll do it.

543
00:21:08,033 --> 00:21:10,833
(goofy laughter)

544
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:11,667
- Oh, not the eyelids.

545
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:12,600
Oh, oh I hate that.

546
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,100
- All right, can I go now?

547
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:17,400
- Oh no, you must do for us

548
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,767
a hand stand.
- Yeah.

549
00:21:18,767 --> 00:21:20,933
- Okay, if I do a
handstand can I go then?

550
00:21:20,933 --> 00:21:22,200
- Oh, of course.

551
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,167
- All right sure,
let's try it here.

552
00:21:23,167 --> 00:21:24,600
All right, ready?

553
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:27,033
Hand stand on the
count of three.

554
00:21:27,033 --> 00:21:29,400
Three, two, one and oh.

555
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:32,367
- Oh, cool.

556
00:21:32,367 --> 00:21:33,600
- [Joel] How's that, you guys?

557
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,467
- Shoes untied.

558
00:21:34,467 --> 00:21:36,667
- Okay and down.

559
00:21:39,133 --> 00:21:40,367
- Great handstand.
- There.

560
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:41,567
All right, I'm gonna
go the galley now.

561
00:21:41,567 --> 00:21:42,800
You guys want anything?

562
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,767
- Yes, human.

563
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:45,067
Well, now that you mention it,

564
00:21:45,067 --> 00:21:46,367
ravioli would be nice.

565
00:21:46,367 --> 00:21:47,233
- Ravioli, okay.
- Yeah and uh,

566
00:21:47,233 --> 00:21:48,500
I'd like a club sandwich

567
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,033
oh and could you
pull the extra bread

568
00:21:50,033 --> 00:21:50,867
out of the middle?

569
00:21:50,867 --> 00:21:52,167
I hate that.

570
00:21:52,167 --> 00:21:53,767
- Okay, no problem,
I'll see you around.

571
00:21:53,767 --> 00:21:55,033
- I love dinner theater.

572
00:21:55,033 --> 00:21:56,867
- Yeah, you know it, pal.

573
00:21:56,867 --> 00:21:59,400
(upbeat music)

574
00:22:06,267 --> 00:22:07,967
- [Dark One] And now, old man.

575
00:22:07,967 --> 00:22:08,967
- [Joel] All right,
all right, here we go.

576
00:22:08,967 --> 00:22:10,100
- [Dark One] Who are you?

577
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,867
- I am a but a
simple man, Dark One.

578
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:15,533
A man who is clearly no
match for your powers.

579
00:22:15,533 --> 00:22:19,300
- [Dark One] And yet you
breathe the poisoned air.

580
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:21,700
- I have no explanation.

581
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:23,233
- [Dark One] Perhaps a
visit to the power station

582
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:25,033
will loosen your tongue?

583
00:22:25,033 --> 00:22:26,267
(Crow blowing raspberries)

584
00:22:26,267 --> 00:22:27,367
Torque, take him.

585
00:22:34,467 --> 00:22:35,600
- And no dinner.

586
00:22:43,833 --> 00:22:45,033
- [Joel] Hey, she
didn't say anything.

587
00:22:45,033 --> 00:22:47,000
- Who are you to keep
me from my father?

588
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:47,833
- Dave.

589
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:50,867
- [Klyton] His name is Neo.

590
00:22:50,867 --> 00:22:53,867
He comes from the
wastelands beyond the city.

591
00:22:53,867 --> 00:22:55,800
- You are immune to
the poisoned air?

592
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,367
- [Klyton] He can live anywhere.

593
00:22:57,367 --> 00:22:58,967
On New Terra.

594
00:22:58,967 --> 00:23:00,933
- Why must we
listen to a freebot

595
00:23:00,933 --> 00:23:02,533
instead of the man himself?

596
00:23:02,533 --> 00:23:05,333
- [Klyton] He speaks
to me telepathically.

597
00:23:05,333 --> 00:23:07,000
- [Servo] Actually, it's
more tele-pathetic-ly.

598
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,833
- [Klyton] He's sure that
you will side with him.

599
00:23:09,833 --> 00:23:11,467
- If he aims to
defeat the Dark One,

600
00:23:11,467 --> 00:23:13,500
we stand with him.

601
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:15,067
- And you.

602
00:23:15,067 --> 00:23:16,400
- My father is in danger,

603
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:17,567
what do you want of me?

604
00:23:17,567 --> 00:23:19,067
- Just five minutes
of your time.

605
00:23:19,067 --> 00:23:21,367
I know you haven't really
considered aluminum siding.

606
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,233
- Not effected.

607
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:25,200
- My father is a scientist.

608
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,133
(Crow and Servo grunting dumbly)

609
00:23:26,133 --> 00:23:27,633
He has created a small device

610
00:23:27,633 --> 00:23:30,267
which subverts the Dark
One's atmosphere control.

611
00:23:31,433 --> 00:23:33,600
He only had time to
create one for himself

612
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:36,000
and me before he was taken away.

613
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,600
- [Joel] They're real expensive.

614
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:40,500
Oh, she's wearing a bell tone.

615
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:42,267
- [Crow] Ew, cooties.

616
00:23:42,267 --> 00:23:44,667
- These work yards
used to house something

617
00:23:44,667 --> 00:23:46,533
called subway system.

618
00:23:46,533 --> 00:23:49,367
- [Servo] They used to be
in things called cities.

619
00:23:49,367 --> 00:23:51,533
- Set up his shop in
one of these rooms.

620
00:23:51,533 --> 00:23:54,000
Now that the device
has been perfected

621
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,333
he said that we could
all be fitted for one

622
00:23:56,333 --> 00:23:58,200
within the next few days.

623
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:00,133
- They would work in
the wastelands as well?

624
00:24:00,133 --> 00:24:01,333
- [All] Shut up.

625
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:03,300
- I have been sent here
by the Rebel society

626
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:05,433
from what you call
the wastelands.

627
00:24:05,433 --> 00:24:09,767
We are organizing an army
to destroy the Dark One

628
00:24:09,767 --> 00:24:11,667
and his forces at
the power station.

629
00:24:11,667 --> 00:24:14,300
- [Klyton] Do you swear
you allegiance Nero?

630
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:15,667
- Hey, it's a young
Robin Williams

631
00:24:15,667 --> 00:24:17,300
on right there right there.

632
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:19,167
- [Klyton] And rescue
your scientist.

633
00:24:20,467 --> 00:24:23,867
- So your tribe is some
kind of hybrid race?

634
00:24:23,867 --> 00:24:25,200
- [Joel] Yeah, you
could say that.

635
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,267
- You could say that.

636
00:24:27,367 --> 00:24:29,733
Our number grows each day.

637
00:24:29,733 --> 00:24:30,967
- [Joel] Thanks to me.

638
00:24:30,967 --> 00:24:33,733
- Now that you know
of my father's device,

639
00:24:33,733 --> 00:24:37,000
you need us as much
as we need you.

640
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:37,933
- And vice versa.

641
00:24:37,933 --> 00:24:39,367
- We don't need the device.

642
00:24:39,367 --> 00:24:40,200
You do.

643
00:24:41,667 --> 00:24:43,133
But an army of Airslaves

644
00:24:43,133 --> 00:24:44,667
who are no longer
really Airslaves...

645
00:24:44,667 --> 00:24:46,967
- [Servo] I can't believe
they cut away to me again.

646
00:24:46,967 --> 00:24:48,100
Get the camera off me.

647
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:49,500
- I am looking for a friend.

648
00:24:50,733 --> 00:24:52,233
- [Joel] The odds
aren't too good.

649
00:24:52,233 --> 00:24:53,500
- I think he's at
the power station.

650
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:55,167
Together, we will go there

651
00:24:55,167 --> 00:24:58,633
and regain control
of the last city

652
00:24:58,633 --> 00:25:00,733
and New Terra.

653
00:25:00,733 --> 00:25:04,700
(tense orchestral music)

654
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:06,400
- [Narrator] And so
the new band of rebels

655
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,500
set out on their journey...

656
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:08,733
- [Servo] Who is that guy?

657
00:25:08,733 --> 00:25:10,133
- [Narrator] Towards
the power station.

658
00:25:10,133 --> 00:25:12,067
- They started at a
landfill outside Manhattan.

659
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:13,333
- [Narrator] Wastelands.

660
00:25:13,333 --> 00:25:16,767
(tense orchestral music)

661
00:25:19,933 --> 00:25:21,933
♪ Take my hand ♪

662
00:25:21,933 --> 00:25:24,733
- [Joel] I'm a
stranger in paradise.

663
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:28,133
(tense orchestral music)

664
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,033
- [Servo] I mean, I
guess it's a wasteland

665
00:25:33,033 --> 00:25:35,500
if you don't count that
big city behind you.

666
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:37,000
- Go to the UN building.

667
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,333
It's filled with
people, behind you.

668
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:45,067
- [Joel] Maybe they're looking
for the Renaissance festival.

669
00:25:48,467 --> 00:25:50,567
- [Servo] And over here we did
Shakespeare in the slag heap.

670
00:25:50,567 --> 00:25:51,700
It was very nice.

671
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,467
- Follow the yellow brick road.

672
00:25:54,467 --> 00:25:55,933
- [Servo] Follow the
yellow brick road.

673
00:25:55,933 --> 00:25:57,800
- [Narrator] Strange mutants
live in the wastelands.

674
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,133
Posing a threat.

675
00:25:59,133 --> 00:26:00,767
- [Servo] The
shrubbery is alive.

676
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:03,633
- [Joel] They finally
found the path again.

677
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:06,967
If I was skeptical, I'd
say that was Central Park.

678
00:26:16,667 --> 00:26:18,267
- Hey, look at this.

679
00:26:18,267 --> 00:26:20,133
- It says this is
not a men's room.

680
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:23,067
- [Joel] I think it
says no graphics.

681
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:26,033
- [Servo] Look,
it's the Bangles.

682
00:26:28,367 --> 00:26:31,000
- [Joel] No it's the
roadshow of Cats.

683
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,800
- They're at the Winter Garden.

684
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:35,500
- [Servo] I'll be
back again and again.

685
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:40,033
(goofy whirring)

686
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,267
- [Joel] Ah, here's my mark.

687
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:43,367
- Here's mine.

688
00:26:43,367 --> 00:26:44,633
- [Servo] Hey, that's my mark.

689
00:26:44,633 --> 00:26:45,567
- [Joel] And I'm here.

690
00:26:45,567 --> 00:26:47,300
Everybody stay on camera.

691
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:48,867
- Don't go for your weapons.

692
00:26:48,867 --> 00:26:51,367
- Who is this woman who
walks through this She Zone

693
00:26:51,367 --> 00:26:53,000
with male scum?

694
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,000
- The woman is with us.

695
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,467
- I speak to the woman.

696
00:26:55,467 --> 00:26:57,000
- I walk with these
men on a mission

697
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,433
to save my father.

698
00:26:58,433 --> 00:26:59,700
- Is that Wendy or Lisa?

699
00:26:59,700 --> 00:27:01,267
- Have you no principles?

700
00:27:01,267 --> 00:27:02,567
- I love my father.

701
00:27:02,567 --> 00:27:04,000
These men have
promised to save him.

702
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:06,033
- No man is to be trusted.

703
00:27:06,033 --> 00:27:08,000
- Then how can
your tribe survive?

704
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,900
- We use men to breed with us

705
00:27:09,900 --> 00:27:11,600
to create future warrior women.

706
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:12,533
- [Servo] Cool.

707
00:27:12,533 --> 00:27:13,633
- Then we dispose of them.

708
00:27:13,633 --> 00:27:14,633
- [Servo] Oh.

709
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,767
- Look, he is the last man.

710
00:27:15,767 --> 00:27:16,600
- [Joel] Hey.

711
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:17,500
It's great.

712
00:27:18,933 --> 00:27:21,300
- He has mated with all of
us who are ready to conceive

713
00:27:21,300 --> 00:27:23,500
and he will now be destroyed.

714
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:25,467
- And he has nothing
to say about this?

715
00:27:25,467 --> 00:27:26,667
- [Servo] I think he'd
highly recommended it.

716
00:27:26,667 --> 00:27:27,833
- First thing we do
when we find one of you

717
00:27:27,833 --> 00:27:29,833
is to remove your tongue.

718
00:27:29,833 --> 00:27:31,167
Men chatter so.

719
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:32,500
- You cowardly bitch.

720
00:27:33,633 --> 00:27:35,500
- I would stop if I were you.

721
00:27:35,500 --> 00:27:39,533
- Why, what difference would
the life of one puny man make?

722
00:27:39,533 --> 00:27:43,300
- Perhaps none but there is
a laser pointed at your head.

723
00:27:43,300 --> 00:27:44,300
- Huh?
- Huh?

724
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:48,133
- How do I know
you're not lying?

725
00:27:48,133 --> 00:27:50,567
- There's only one way
to find out, isn't there?

726
00:27:50,567 --> 00:27:51,667
- What do you want?

727
00:27:51,667 --> 00:27:54,167
- A chance for a fair fight.

728
00:27:54,167 --> 00:27:56,400
- [Narrator] A knife is
placed in the ground.

729
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:58,533
- [Servo] A voiceover
is placed in the script.

730
00:27:58,533 --> 00:28:01,333
(tense orchestral music)

731
00:28:01,333 --> 00:28:02,767
- They're gonna play mumbly peg?

732
00:28:05,700 --> 00:28:07,033
- [Joel] I'm gonna cut you man,

733
00:28:07,033 --> 00:28:08,533
I'm gonna cut you real good.

734
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:13,767
- Tear him apart.

735
00:28:13,767 --> 00:28:15,867
- [Joel] You know the
more things change

736
00:28:15,867 --> 00:28:17,733
the more they stay the same?

737
00:28:17,733 --> 00:28:20,167
- [Servo] Yeah like the way
guys and gals get together

738
00:28:20,167 --> 00:28:21,400
and just love.

739
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:23,600
- Central Park hasn't
really changed, either.

740
00:28:25,167 --> 00:28:26,500
- Rip his flesh.

741
00:28:29,967 --> 00:28:30,900
- David Lee Roth.

742
00:28:32,067 --> 00:28:33,633
- [Woman] Kill him!

743
00:28:36,133 --> 00:28:37,800
- Emmett Kelly.

744
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:39,067
- [Servo] Puny man, eh?

745
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:44,100
- By the rules of our
tribe, I belong to you

746
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:45,567
to do what you will with me.

747
00:28:45,567 --> 00:28:46,433
- All right.

748
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:48,100
- What do you suggest?

749
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:49,700
- Kill me because
if I get the chance

750
00:28:49,700 --> 00:28:51,200
I will kill you.

751
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,033
- And why should I kill you?

752
00:28:53,033 --> 00:28:54,967
Your people are like
me, aren't they?

753
00:28:54,967 --> 00:28:56,067
- [Servo] Look at that,
she's stuffing Kleenex,

754
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:57,033
look at that.

755
00:28:57,033 --> 00:28:57,900
- You can breathe the air.

756
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:58,833
- The Dark One?

757
00:28:58,833 --> 00:28:59,633
- What a time to get a cold.

758
00:28:59,633 --> 00:29:00,733
- We don't fear him.

759
00:29:00,733 --> 00:29:02,467
He sends transbots to tame us

760
00:29:02,467 --> 00:29:04,000
and we cut them into scrap.

761
00:29:05,267 --> 00:29:07,733
- Your ancestors came
from the wasteland.

762
00:29:07,733 --> 00:29:08,900
- We have no history.

763
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:10,600
We have always been here.

764
00:29:10,600 --> 00:29:11,833
- So you have a history?

765
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,467
- Others who can exist
here without the device?

766
00:29:13,467 --> 00:29:14,767
- Only Nyla's woman.

767
00:29:14,767 --> 00:29:16,667
We've heard stories of them.

768
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:20,567
You can help lead us
to the power station.

769
00:29:20,567 --> 00:29:22,133
- I know where it is.

770
00:29:22,133 --> 00:29:24,533
- Then you will take us to it.

771
00:29:24,533 --> 00:29:25,467
- [Joel] Maybe.

772
00:29:25,467 --> 00:29:26,967
- If that is your desire.

773
00:29:26,967 --> 00:29:29,733
But once my debt to you
is paid, I will kill you.

774
00:29:29,733 --> 00:29:31,033
- If you live that long.

775
00:29:32,233 --> 00:29:33,600
- [Servo] Threats,
threats, threats.

776
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:34,933
- Free the mute, he
will come with us.

777
00:29:34,933 --> 00:29:36,967
- [Nyla] Kai, what
use is he to us?

778
00:29:36,967 --> 00:29:37,800
- [Joel] Hello.

779
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:39,033
- Maybe none.

780
00:29:39,033 --> 00:29:40,000
Sometimes people can
be help for no reason

781
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,100
other than human charity.

782
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:43,067
- [Servo] And he can sign.

783
00:29:43,067 --> 00:29:44,767
- They're all useless and crazy.

784
00:29:49,367 --> 00:29:52,033
(Joel coughing)

785
00:29:55,133 --> 00:29:56,433
- I think I have this calender.

786
00:29:56,433 --> 00:29:57,767
- [Narrator] Deep
in the power station

787
00:29:57,767 --> 00:29:59,900
lies the pleasure machine.

788
00:29:59,900 --> 00:30:00,833
- [Servo] All right.

789
00:30:00,833 --> 00:30:02,100
- [Narrator] A reward for those

790
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:04,600
who loyally serve the Dark One.

791
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,600
(eerie tense music)

792
00:30:12,133 --> 00:30:13,133
(men laughing)

793
00:30:13,133 --> 00:30:14,267
- What?

794
00:30:14,267 --> 00:30:16,933
(eerie tense music)

795
00:30:16,933 --> 00:30:19,500
(upbeat music)

796
00:30:23,833 --> 00:30:25,000
- [Dark One] Valaria.

797
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,167
- Dark One, I--
- The pleasure machine

798
00:30:26,167 --> 00:30:28,400
is to be used as a reward.

799
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:29,733
Not for habit.

800
00:30:29,733 --> 00:30:30,933
- Yes, Dark One.

801
00:30:30,933 --> 00:30:32,033
- [Dark One] It would
serve you well...

802
00:30:32,033 --> 00:30:33,267
- [Servo] Dog one, boog one.

803
00:30:33,267 --> 00:30:35,467
- I--
- The discussion has ended.

804
00:30:35,467 --> 00:30:38,800
There are other
matters to attend to.

805
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,300
- [Servo] Pretty self indulgent

806
00:30:42,300 --> 00:30:43,733
for someone with a
speech impediment.

807
00:30:45,033 --> 00:30:46,233
- [Dark One] Torque
and the guardbots

808
00:30:46,233 --> 00:30:50,000
bring you a new subject
for interrogation.

809
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,333
- Yes, Dark One.

810
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:53,967
- [Joel] Is she
wearing a kitchen mat?

811
00:30:53,967 --> 00:30:54,933
- [Crow] Yeah, she
better not go out

812
00:30:54,933 --> 00:30:56,033
in the sun in that outfit.

813
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:03,733
- Torque, have the man
freed from his bonds.

814
00:31:03,733 --> 00:31:05,000
- James Bond.

815
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,233
- There is no reason for
him to be uncomfortable.

816
00:31:08,233 --> 00:31:09,800
- [Servo] But I kind
of like the chains.

817
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:11,000
You know, you look familiar.

818
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:12,500
We're you in Yards of Leather?

819
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:26,700
- There, isn't that better?

820
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:27,867
- What, your accent?

821
00:31:29,233 --> 00:31:32,300
- It will benefit all
of us if you cooperate.

822
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:34,467
Do you understand?

823
00:31:34,467 --> 00:31:35,600
- [Joel] No, none
of us understand.

824
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:36,800
We don't know

825
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:38,067
what you're saying.
- Can't understand you.

826
00:31:38,067 --> 00:31:40,967
- You are impervious to
our atmosphere control.

827
00:31:40,967 --> 00:31:44,067
- [Joel] Hey, watch who
you call impervious, lady.

828
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:48,767
- Your stay with us
could be quite pleasant

829
00:31:48,767 --> 00:31:50,933
if you choose to work with us.

830
00:31:50,933 --> 00:31:52,300
- [Crow] You mean
you'll stop talking?

831
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:55,067
- On the other hand,
I could introduce you

832
00:31:55,067 --> 00:31:58,467
to worlds of pain
beyond your imagination.

833
00:31:58,467 --> 00:31:59,433
- [Servo] Well, let's just skip

834
00:31:59,433 --> 00:32:00,300
to the worlds of pain, then.

835
00:32:00,300 --> 00:32:01,833
- The choice is yours.

836
00:32:03,033 --> 00:32:05,233
- I have no answers for you.

837
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:07,567
- A pity.

838
00:32:08,667 --> 00:32:10,767
- [Dark One] I am losing
patience, Valaria.

839
00:32:12,267 --> 00:32:13,967
- Torque, take him
to the crystal.

840
00:32:14,967 --> 00:32:16,067
- [Joel] Torque?

841
00:32:16,067 --> 00:32:17,500
Oh that's what
happened to Peter Tork.

842
00:32:17,500 --> 00:32:20,100
He's doing rubber suit work now.

843
00:32:20,100 --> 00:32:21,667
After The Monkees broke up.

844
00:32:21,667 --> 00:32:22,833
That's interesting.

845
00:32:22,833 --> 00:32:25,233
- I knew that haircut
would come back.

846
00:32:25,233 --> 00:32:26,700
- [Narrator] At the crystal,

847
00:32:26,700 --> 00:32:28,767
Jorn can see that the Dark One

848
00:32:28,767 --> 00:32:30,033
is aware of the
rebel's every move.

849
00:32:30,033 --> 00:32:31,600
- [Servo] There's
that guy again.

850
00:32:33,567 --> 00:32:35,700
- She's your
daughter, isn't she?

851
00:32:35,700 --> 00:32:36,633
- [Joel] Maybe.

852
00:32:36,633 --> 00:32:38,467
- Let go of me, muslin face.

853
00:32:40,100 --> 00:32:42,800
- It would be a pity if
she had to lose her life

854
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,733
because of your silence.

855
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:47,800
- I have nothing to say.

856
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:49,167
- [Joel] Uh, except
for what I just said.

857
00:32:49,167 --> 00:32:51,300
- My daughter would
want it that way.

858
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:55,333
- Then your daughter is a
bigger fool than you are.

859
00:32:55,333 --> 00:32:57,433
- [Servo] She could just like
clear her throat or something.

860
00:32:57,433 --> 00:32:59,267
- Torque, take him to
the room of questions.

861
00:32:59,267 --> 00:33:01,267
- Where is the
room of questions?

862
00:33:01,267 --> 00:33:02,667
- [Joel] Would you stop that?

863
00:33:02,667 --> 00:33:04,600
Don't even start.

864
00:33:04,600 --> 00:33:05,433
Hey, wait for me.

865
00:33:06,300 --> 00:33:07,900
- We will see just how long

866
00:33:07,900 --> 00:33:11,367
he can keep his
secrets to himself.

867
00:33:11,367 --> 00:33:13,767
- [Dark One] Your work is
cut out for you, Valaria.

868
00:33:13,767 --> 00:33:15,200
- [Servo] Your dress
is cut out for you.

869
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:16,267
- Dark One.
- Stock watt?

870
00:33:16,267 --> 00:33:17,567
- Stock worm?

871
00:33:17,567 --> 00:33:18,933
- Yes, Dark One.

872
00:33:18,933 --> 00:33:20,000
- [Joel] Stock one.

873
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,400
- [Servo] Duck bun, I think.

874
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:23,633
- [Joel] Beats me.

875
00:33:23,633 --> 00:33:25,433
- See how we fused
this grown cover

876
00:33:25,433 --> 00:33:27,067
to halt the erosion
on this hill?

877
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,300
- There.

878
00:33:29,300 --> 00:33:30,300
- What is it?

879
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:32,067
- The caverns start here.

880
00:33:32,067 --> 00:33:33,333
- Caverns?

881
00:33:33,333 --> 00:33:34,167
- [Servo] Yes, caverns.

882
00:33:34,167 --> 00:33:35,400
Like between your ears.

883
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:36,767
- The power station
from underground.

884
00:33:36,767 --> 00:33:40,067
The Dark One has ways of
monitoring our progress

885
00:33:40,067 --> 00:33:41,567
if we continue on the surface.

886
00:33:42,567 --> 00:33:43,933
Come.

887
00:33:43,933 --> 00:33:45,633
- [Joel] I hate
when he does that.

888
00:33:49,133 --> 00:33:51,233
- [Narrator] The mutants
continued to follow the rebels

889
00:33:51,233 --> 00:33:53,500
even as they entered
the underground caverns.

890
00:33:53,500 --> 00:33:55,567
- Hey, it's Shelley Duvall.

891
00:33:55,567 --> 00:33:58,033
(tense music)

892
00:34:01,367 --> 00:34:03,300
- We must be quiet
from here on in.

893
00:34:03,300 --> 00:34:04,233
- Why?

894
00:34:04,233 --> 00:34:05,000
- [Crow] Writer's strike.

895
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:05,900
- Sewage worms.

896
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:06,767
- [Crow] Same thing.

897
00:34:06,767 --> 00:34:08,400
- What?
- Sewage worms.

898
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,600
Man eating creatures
from this tribal void.

899
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:11,833
(Joel chuckling)

900
00:34:11,833 --> 00:34:12,767
- They look like.
- They're blind

901
00:34:12,767 --> 00:34:14,033
but they seek their prey..

902
00:34:14,033 --> 00:34:15,267
- [Joel] Pink socks
with teeth in ''em.

903
00:34:15,267 --> 00:34:17,367
- [Klyton] Humans,
they eat humans.

904
00:34:17,367 --> 00:34:19,133
- [Servo] How 'bout
a show of hands?

905
00:34:19,133 --> 00:34:22,967
(creatures snarling)

906
00:34:22,967 --> 00:34:24,700
- This is their nest.

907
00:34:24,700 --> 00:34:26,700
If we can get to the other side,

908
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:27,833
we'll be safe.

909
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:28,767
- Safe?

910
00:34:28,767 --> 00:34:30,100
We'll never make it through.

911
00:34:30,100 --> 00:34:31,567
- What kind of a woman are you?

912
00:34:31,567 --> 00:34:33,033
Have you no fighting spirit?

913
00:34:33,033 --> 00:34:34,133
- Enough.

914
00:34:34,133 --> 00:34:36,033
Let's see how many there are.

915
00:34:36,033 --> 00:34:38,533
(tense music)

916
00:34:40,733 --> 00:34:42,900
- He's carrying a
giant beef stick.

917
00:34:47,633 --> 00:34:48,567
It's Kukla!

918
00:34:48,567 --> 00:34:49,800
- How can we make it through?

919
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,367
- If only we had
some kind of bait

920
00:34:51,367 --> 00:34:52,800
to distract them while the rest

921
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,900
of us slipped through.

922
00:34:54,767 --> 00:34:56,367
- [Joel] Bait, sock bait?

923
00:34:56,367 --> 00:35:00,867
- [Klyton] Will surely
be attacked by the worms.

924
00:35:00,867 --> 00:35:04,800
- [Servo] You can't make
me, you can't make me.

925
00:35:06,100 --> 00:35:07,633
- Kukla, buddy.

926
00:35:09,367 --> 00:35:11,900
- [Joel] Sock broke
my beef stick.

927
00:35:11,900 --> 00:35:12,733
I can't believe it.

928
00:35:12,733 --> 00:35:13,633
Look at this.

929
00:35:13,633 --> 00:35:14,867
He broke my beef stick.

930
00:35:14,867 --> 00:35:15,667
- [Servo] Which one
of them is Ginger

931
00:35:15,667 --> 00:35:17,167
and which is Mary-Ann?

932
00:35:17,167 --> 00:35:18,567
- There's only one way.

933
00:35:18,567 --> 00:35:19,500
- What?

934
00:35:19,500 --> 00:35:20,800
- We chop our way through.

935
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:21,967
- Yes!

936
00:35:21,967 --> 00:35:22,800
- Ready?

937
00:35:25,233 --> 00:35:26,067
Now.

938
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:30,000
(goofy tense music)

939
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,533
(shouting)

940
00:35:32,533 --> 00:35:33,467
- Oh, wow.

941
00:35:33,467 --> 00:35:36,033
He got smeared with Rust-Oleum.

942
00:35:36,033 --> 00:35:36,867
- [Servo] What a
time to be caught

943
00:35:36,867 --> 00:35:38,233
without a turtleneck.

944
00:35:38,233 --> 00:35:39,700
- [Joel] I don't think my socks

945
00:35:39,700 --> 00:35:41,133
have ever gotten that bad.

946
00:35:44,367 --> 00:35:45,467
- [Servo] Ew.

947
00:35:47,367 --> 00:35:48,200
- Egg rolls.

948
00:35:50,900 --> 00:35:51,900
- [Klyton] Stop it, worms.

949
00:35:51,900 --> 00:35:53,067
I'm not human.

950
00:35:55,833 --> 00:35:57,667
- [Joel] Hey, Chippa.

951
00:35:57,667 --> 00:35:59,600
- You owe me one, woman.

952
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,433
- So now it's two women?

953
00:36:02,567 --> 00:36:04,333
- I pay my debts quick.

954
00:36:04,333 --> 00:36:05,833
- Now it's back to one woman.

955
00:36:05,833 --> 00:36:07,733
- [Servo] This whole movie
is just socks and violence.

956
00:36:07,733 --> 00:36:11,000
(tense music)

957
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:13,500
- [Klyton] Just go away.

958
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:14,433
- [Servo] At least
it's some good work

959
00:36:14,433 --> 00:36:15,800
for the out of work hand models.

960
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,300
(tense music)

961
00:36:21,633 --> 00:36:22,933
- [Joel] Hey, don't
touch my hair.

962
00:36:22,933 --> 00:36:24,467
I worked real hard on that hair.

963
00:36:24,467 --> 00:36:25,733
- You have saved
me a second time.

964
00:36:25,733 --> 00:36:26,667
- [Klyton] Now you
can be his friend.

965
00:36:26,667 --> 00:36:28,333
- So it's two again?

966
00:36:28,333 --> 00:36:30,500
- I owe allegiance to no man.

967
00:36:30,500 --> 00:36:31,633
- [Crow] One.

968
00:36:31,633 --> 00:36:33,100
- No allegiance.

969
00:36:33,100 --> 00:36:35,867
Only your help in leading
us to our destination.

970
00:36:36,900 --> 00:36:38,767
- An oasis lies ahead.

971
00:36:38,767 --> 00:36:40,600
There we can rest.

972
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:43,367
- And you can get those
little cow cream pitchers.

973
00:36:43,367 --> 00:36:45,267
- [Klyton] What I
need is a tune up.

974
00:36:45,267 --> 00:36:47,000
- [Joel] Dudes, totally
awesome job in there.

975
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,700
Really coming
together as a group.

976
00:36:55,300 --> 00:36:56,967
- [Klyton] Look
at all this water.

977
00:36:56,967 --> 00:36:59,333
It's sure to rust
my microcircuits.

978
00:36:59,333 --> 00:37:00,667
- [All] Shut up.

979
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:09,600
- [Servo] Hey, this doesn't
look like the brochure.

980
00:37:09,600 --> 00:37:11,700
There was supposed to
be a tennis court here.

981
00:37:13,833 --> 00:37:14,867
- What's down in there?

982
00:37:14,867 --> 00:37:16,200
- Bean fish.

983
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:18,267
- You don't want to know.

984
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:22,133
- [Joel] It looks
like a lava lamp.

985
00:37:22,133 --> 00:37:23,700
Oh, it's the Dark One.

986
00:37:23,700 --> 00:37:25,133
- [Dark One] Continue
on their way to us.

987
00:37:25,133 --> 00:37:26,300
- [Servo] The dag wah.

988
00:37:26,300 --> 00:37:28,367
- The rebels,
they're still alive.

989
00:37:28,367 --> 00:37:30,867
They must have
the immunity, too.

990
00:37:30,867 --> 00:37:32,100
- [Dark One] Perhaps.

991
00:37:32,100 --> 00:37:34,633
No matter, is better
that they still live.

992
00:37:34,633 --> 00:37:35,467
- Better?

993
00:37:35,467 --> 00:37:36,667
- [Dark One] Yes.

994
00:37:36,667 --> 00:37:39,100
We can use the girl's
life as (mumbles)

995
00:37:39,100 --> 00:37:40,500
or her death.

996
00:37:40,500 --> 00:37:43,267
- She looks like the
new Lily Munster.

997
00:37:43,267 --> 00:37:44,867
- We have nothing to fear.

998
00:37:44,867 --> 00:37:46,133
- But fear itself.

999
00:37:46,133 --> 00:37:48,100
- Before the might
of our transbots.

1000
00:37:48,100 --> 00:37:49,833
- [Dark One] Have you forgotten?

1001
00:37:49,833 --> 00:37:52,367
The warrior woman has destroyed

1002
00:37:52,367 --> 00:37:54,367
a number of our best units.

1003
00:37:56,967 --> 00:38:00,433
- Perhaps, it is
time to send Torque.

1004
00:38:00,433 --> 00:38:03,167
- [Dark One] You have made
the right decisions, Valaria.

1005
00:38:03,167 --> 00:38:05,300
- [Joel] Then send
Olands and Nesmith, too.

1006
00:38:10,767 --> 00:38:13,167
- Has the man revealed
anything to you?

1007
00:38:13,167 --> 00:38:14,967
- Just his hernia scar.

1008
00:38:14,967 --> 00:38:16,467
- [Torque] His will is strong.

1009
00:38:17,333 --> 00:38:19,233
- What power have you used?

1010
00:38:19,233 --> 00:38:21,733
- [Torque] We have
taken him twice.

1011
00:38:21,733 --> 00:38:22,667
- [Joel] You know, he's great.

1012
00:38:22,667 --> 00:38:24,233
You never see his lips move.

1013
00:38:24,233 --> 00:38:25,867
- Seven?

1014
00:38:25,867 --> 00:38:28,000
He's to be reckoned with.

1015
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,800
Take him to nine.

1016
00:38:30,967 --> 00:38:33,300
- [Servo] Number
nine, number nine.

1017
00:38:33,300 --> 00:38:34,733
Number nine.

1018
00:38:34,733 --> 00:38:37,933
(electricity crackling)
(groaning)

1019
00:38:37,933 --> 00:38:38,767
- Revive him.

1020
00:38:38,767 --> 00:38:39,700
I need him awake.

1021
00:38:42,767 --> 00:38:44,400
- [Servo] Revive with Vyvern.

1022
00:38:48,333 --> 00:38:51,300
- How can you breathe
the poisoned air?

1023
00:38:51,300 --> 00:38:53,300
- Well, I ran a Mexican
restaurant for awhile

1024
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:55,867
than I worked in the
primate house at the zoo.

1025
00:38:55,867 --> 00:38:58,400
- Torque, you are to
leave the power station

1026
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:01,433
and intercept the group
that approaches us

1027
00:39:01,433 --> 00:39:04,200
and when you reach them,
the first thing you are

1028
00:39:04,200 --> 00:39:07,800
to do is kill the girl.

1029
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:08,867
Do you understand?

1030
00:39:08,867 --> 00:39:10,300
- [Torque] Yes.

1031
00:39:10,300 --> 00:39:12,633
- Do you understand, old man?

1032
00:39:12,633 --> 00:39:14,500
- [Servo] Yeah, it's young
