00:49:20,500 --> 00:49:22,567
If we stop bringing fuel
to the power station

1283
00:49:22,567 --> 00:49:24,733
the Dark One will have
no power to control us.

1284
00:49:24,733 --> 00:49:26,100
- Are you mad?

1285
00:49:26,100 --> 00:49:27,667
If the Dark One
hears of what you say

1286
00:49:27,667 --> 00:49:28,833
we will all die.

1287
00:49:28,833 --> 00:49:30,500
- Korla, hear me.

1288
00:49:30,500 --> 00:49:32,567
- [Servo] Listen to me,
I was in Godspell once.

1289
00:49:32,567 --> 00:49:34,200
- If the warrior and
Deeja still live.

1290
00:49:34,200 --> 00:49:36,733
- Hey that guy behind him
got his headphones on wrong.

1291
00:49:36,733 --> 00:49:37,633
- Not us.

1292
00:49:37,633 --> 00:49:38,833
- So?

1293
00:49:38,833 --> 00:49:40,733
- So, we will go
through the motions

1294
00:49:40,733 --> 00:49:42,400
of bringing fuel
to the machines.

1295
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:44,600
If the powers of the
Dark One monitor us

1296
00:49:44,600 --> 00:49:45,900
they will see us working.

1297
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:46,900
- And?

1298
00:49:46,900 --> 00:49:48,667
- And we will bring...

1299
00:49:48,667 --> 00:49:49,867
- [Joel] Isn't he
wearing the shirt

1300
00:49:49,867 --> 00:49:51,767
that Brando wore in
Streetcar Named Desire?

1301
00:49:51,767 --> 00:49:52,600
- Yup.

1302
00:49:58,133 --> 00:49:59,300
- [Dark One] What do you see?

1303
00:49:59,300 --> 00:50:00,800
- A five dollar globe lamp.

1304
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:02,800
- They are in the
vault of beats.

1305
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:04,300
- [Servo] The walls of Greece?

1306
00:50:04,300 --> 00:50:06,300
- [Joel] No, it's not that.

1307
00:50:06,300 --> 00:50:08,733
- [Dark One] What
of the Airslaves?

1308
00:50:08,733 --> 00:50:10,667
- [Servo] It's not easy
growing the best potatoes

1309
00:50:10,667 --> 00:50:12,233
in the world but it's worth it.

1310
00:50:16,500 --> 00:50:18,533
- Their work
continues, Dark One.

1311
00:50:18,533 --> 00:50:20,033
- [Dark One] Good.

1312
00:50:20,033 --> 00:50:22,833
Make sure Torque
tends to our visitor.

1313
00:50:22,833 --> 00:50:24,567
- As you command.

1314
00:50:24,567 --> 00:50:25,700
- [Joel] You know, they
got a lot of heat loss

1315
00:50:25,700 --> 00:50:26,967
coming out of that computer.

1316
00:50:26,967 --> 00:50:28,600
A little caulking
would really help.

1317
00:50:29,633 --> 00:50:31,233
- Caulking?

1318
00:50:31,233 --> 00:50:34,233
(tense music)

1319
00:50:34,233 --> 00:50:36,000
- Hey, Cleveland.
- Rock and roll.

1320
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:37,333
- [Joel] Let's do it.

1321
00:50:37,333 --> 00:50:39,800
(tense music)

1322
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:42,967
- Hey, crustacean head.

1323
00:50:46,633 --> 00:50:48,067
- [Servo] Huh?

1324
00:50:48,067 --> 00:50:51,267
(tense dramatic music)

1325
00:50:58,467 --> 00:50:59,333
Hey, could you get my lighter

1326
00:50:59,333 --> 00:51:01,100
when you're down there?

1327
00:51:01,100 --> 00:51:02,633
- Come on, you gold bricker.

1328
00:51:02,633 --> 00:51:04,233
Get up, you're not hurt.

1329
00:51:04,233 --> 00:51:05,467
Come on, shake it off.

1330
00:51:06,500 --> 00:51:07,333
You wuss.

1331
00:51:11,500 --> 00:51:12,833
- [Joel] All right, folks.

1332
00:51:12,833 --> 00:51:15,967
Back it up, give 'em
some air, everybody.

1333
00:51:15,967 --> 00:51:17,867
Come on, he's gonna be okay.

1334
00:51:17,867 --> 00:51:18,700
Shows over.

1335
00:51:18,700 --> 00:51:20,167
Everybody go home.

1336
00:51:20,167 --> 00:51:21,000
Go home.

1337
00:51:23,900 --> 00:51:25,467
- [Servo] Hey, guys,
watch that first step,

1338
00:51:25,467 --> 00:51:26,533
it's a doozy.

1339
00:51:30,967 --> 00:51:33,700
- [Joel] Now, that's
unfortunate skin right there.

1340
00:51:35,533 --> 00:51:37,267
- [Servo] He's the craw daddy.

1341
00:51:37,267 --> 00:51:38,900
- Hey, he'd be great
with drawn butter.

1342
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:40,033
- [Servo] Or cocktail sauce.

1343
00:51:40,033 --> 00:51:42,167
- He's a crust-tafarian.

1344
00:51:42,167 --> 00:51:43,433
- [Servo] You know, you
serve him with red red wine.

1345
00:51:43,433 --> 00:51:44,467
- [Joel] Okay, okay.

1346
00:51:44,467 --> 00:51:45,267
- [Servo] Sorry.

1347
00:51:46,633 --> 00:51:47,800
- [Joel] Is that her tail?

1348
00:51:47,800 --> 00:51:49,133
- No, she just
played with her stick

1349
00:51:49,133 --> 00:51:50,100
until it frayed.

1350
00:51:52,233 --> 00:51:53,067
- [Servo] Her dress
looks like something

1351
00:51:53,067 --> 00:51:54,633
they cut gaskets out of.

1352
00:51:56,067 --> 00:51:57,700
- [Dark One] His will
is powerful, Valaria.

1353
00:51:58,933 --> 00:52:02,133
- No one is a match for
your strength, Dark One.

1354
00:52:02,133 --> 00:52:03,767
- Dogma?

1355
00:52:03,767 --> 00:52:06,400
- [Dark One] There is only
one way for him to know.

1356
00:52:06,400 --> 00:52:07,533
- Yes?

1357
00:52:08,700 --> 00:52:11,667
- [Dark One] Let
him join with me!

1358
00:52:11,667 --> 00:52:14,267
- [Joel] Just wait till this
jet goes over, Dark One.

1359
00:52:14,267 --> 00:52:17,100
(low rumbling)

1360
00:52:17,100 --> 00:52:19,000
- [Servo] Wait till this
commercial goes over.

1361
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:20,033
- [Joel] Will it go over?

1362
00:52:20,033 --> 00:52:22,100
(low rumbling)

1363
00:52:22,100 --> 00:52:23,967
- [Servo] Go over great.

1364
00:52:23,967 --> 00:52:25,800
- [Joel] Hello, Cleveland.

1365
00:52:25,800 --> 00:52:26,867
Rock and roll.

1366
00:52:28,033 --> 00:52:30,500
Let's do it, Cleveland.

1367
00:52:30,500 --> 00:52:33,500
(suspenseful music)

1368
00:52:34,367 --> 00:52:35,533
- [Servo] Huh?

1369
00:52:36,700 --> 00:52:38,100
- How did the creature die?

1370
00:52:38,100 --> 00:52:41,200
- [Klyton] We are not
alone in these tunnels.

1371
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:42,833
- Keep your weapons
at the ready.

1372
00:52:42,833 --> 00:52:44,367
- We could be next.

1373
00:52:44,367 --> 00:52:45,467
- Not if we remain alert.

1374
00:52:45,467 --> 00:52:46,300
Come on.

1375
00:52:48,233 --> 00:52:50,067
- [Servo] Aren't they
the kids from Fame?

1376
00:52:52,100 --> 00:52:53,867
- They're gonna dance forever.

1377
00:52:57,367 --> 00:52:58,833
We're gonna learn how to cry.

1378
00:53:00,833 --> 00:53:03,033
- [Servo] Just hope they
don't get to a lunchroom.

1379
00:53:05,733 --> 00:53:07,100
- [Joel] Oh, hi ya, crusty.

1380
00:53:07,100 --> 00:53:08,600
- Hello, lady face.

1381
00:53:08,600 --> 00:53:11,200
- Why would you kill of
one of the inferior beings

1382
00:53:11,200 --> 00:53:13,033
instead of the girl?

1383
00:53:13,033 --> 00:53:15,467
- [Torque] Their path
away from the body

1384
00:53:15,467 --> 00:53:18,867
now leads them to
the beast of the web.

1385
00:53:19,767 --> 00:53:21,300
- A Cylon wannabee.

1386
00:53:21,300 --> 00:53:25,300
- Torque, your programming is
more advanced than I thought.

1387
00:53:25,300 --> 00:53:26,233
- [Joel] Do you think so?

1388
00:53:26,233 --> 00:53:27,800
I've really been working on it.

1389
00:53:27,800 --> 00:53:28,733
- [Torque] To retrieve the girl?

1390
00:53:28,733 --> 00:53:31,667
- No, not now, it is too late.

1391
00:53:31,667 --> 00:53:33,400
Whatever information we need

1392
00:53:33,400 --> 00:53:35,133
will come from the Dark One.

1393
00:53:35,133 --> 00:53:36,367
- [Servo] The dart board?

1394
00:53:36,367 --> 00:53:39,400
- He has joined with
the girl's father.

1395
00:53:39,400 --> 00:53:41,567
- [Torque] The others?

1396
00:53:41,567 --> 00:53:43,867
- If you have lead them
in the right direction

1397
00:53:43,867 --> 00:53:46,867
they will no longer
be of concern to us.

1398
00:53:46,867 --> 00:53:47,967
- Huh?
- What?

1399
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:57,667
- [Joel] Hey,
wouldn't it be funny

1400
00:53:57,667 --> 00:53:59,800
if they ran into master
carpenter, Norm Abram?

1401
00:54:03,800 --> 00:54:05,033
- What we're doing here, Bob,

1402
00:54:05,033 --> 00:54:07,667
is we got this
little robot problem.

1403
00:54:09,467 --> 00:54:11,533
- [Servo] They look like
Heart, the rock group.

1404
00:54:11,533 --> 00:54:12,467
- [Joel] Kinda.

1405
00:54:12,467 --> 00:54:13,800
The Wilson sisters there.

1406
00:54:13,800 --> 00:54:14,733
- [Servo] Oh yeah.

1407
00:54:14,733 --> 00:54:15,933
- Why was that mutant killed

1408
00:54:15,933 --> 00:54:17,200
and why was it right
in front of us?

1409
00:54:17,200 --> 00:54:18,833
- [Klyton] It was a warning.

1410
00:54:18,833 --> 00:54:19,667
- a warning?

1411
00:54:21,133 --> 00:54:22,767
- [Klyton] A sign that we
should not go any further.

1412
00:54:22,767 --> 00:54:24,333
- Ah, you got blemish there.

1413
00:54:24,333 --> 00:54:25,833
- [Servo] It's a Robo Shankar.

1414
00:54:26,767 --> 00:54:27,733
- [Klyton] The Dark One.

1415
00:54:27,733 --> 00:54:28,900
- Dark One?

1416
00:54:28,900 --> 00:54:30,167
But why?

1417
00:54:30,167 --> 00:54:31,167
- He used to play
with the Beatles.

1418
00:54:31,167 --> 00:54:32,000
- Want to stop us.

1419
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:33,667
- [Servo] Robo Shankar?

1420
00:54:33,667 --> 00:54:36,133
- Perhaps we knows
we are immune.

1421
00:54:36,133 --> 00:54:37,767
- Not all of us.

1422
00:54:37,767 --> 00:54:39,467
- Some of us are equity.

1423
00:54:39,467 --> 00:54:40,400
- Well I hope not.

1424
00:54:40,400 --> 00:54:41,800
Kai is unprotected and so am I.

1425
00:54:41,800 --> 00:54:43,400
- Well, the rest of us are fine

1426
00:54:43,400 --> 00:54:44,400
and since you are just men,

1427
00:54:44,400 --> 00:54:45,667
what difference does it make?

1428
00:54:45,667 --> 00:54:46,933
- [Joel] Hey, I think
somebody's forgetting

1429
00:54:46,933 --> 00:54:48,933
who's holding the pink
slip, little lady.

1430
00:54:48,933 --> 00:54:50,833
- Lowest excuse for a
human I have ever met.

1431
00:54:50,833 --> 00:54:51,667
(grunting)

1432
00:54:51,667 --> 00:54:52,967
- [Servo] Cat fight.

1433
00:54:52,967 --> 00:54:54,600
- There is no time for this.

1434
00:54:54,600 --> 00:54:56,600
- Neo!
- You mean duck?

1435
00:54:56,600 --> 00:54:57,433
- Help.

1436
00:54:58,500 --> 00:55:00,500
- Don't everybody move at once.

1437
00:55:00,500 --> 00:55:01,433
- What?

1438
00:55:01,433 --> 00:55:04,000
- [Klyton] The beast of the web.

1439
00:55:04,000 --> 00:55:07,433
Come, there are only
moments to save her.

1440
00:55:07,433 --> 00:55:09,933
(tense music)

1441
00:55:10,900 --> 00:55:12,733
- [Servo] The itsy bitsy spider

1442
00:55:12,733 --> 00:55:15,367
went up the water spout.

1443
00:55:15,367 --> 00:55:17,267
- [Joel] Hello, Marta.

1444
00:55:17,267 --> 00:55:18,833
- [Servo] Lancelot.

1445
00:55:20,333 --> 00:55:21,167
Lancelot.

1446
00:55:25,467 --> 00:55:26,800
- [Joel] Come back,
you dummkopfs.

1447
00:55:26,800 --> 00:55:28,133
Come back here.

1448
00:55:28,133 --> 00:55:30,633
(tense music)

1449
00:55:32,433 --> 00:55:33,800
- Hey, you left your femur.

1450
00:55:38,867 --> 00:55:40,300
- Night will fall soon, Roan.

1451
00:55:41,200 --> 00:55:42,367
- I know, Korla.

1452
00:55:42,367 --> 00:55:43,800
We must continue.

1453
00:55:43,800 --> 00:55:45,367
- But they will soon
know at the power station

1454
00:55:45,367 --> 00:55:46,500
that we have not
fueled our share...

1455
00:55:46,500 --> 00:55:47,800
- [Servo] Hey, posture,
buddy, posture.

1456
00:55:47,800 --> 00:55:49,667
- The warrior,
Deeja, and the others

1457
00:55:49,667 --> 00:55:50,633
may still live.

1458
00:55:50,633 --> 00:55:51,967
- What good can come of that?

1459
00:55:51,967 --> 00:55:54,200
- Well, my friend has
Bob Fosse's home number.

1460
00:55:54,200 --> 00:55:56,867
- Their might could be
stronger than the Dark One's.

1461
00:55:56,867 --> 00:55:58,133
- How?

1462
00:55:58,133 --> 00:55:59,800
- The Dark One draws his
energy from our labors.

1463
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:01,867
If we provide him
with no energy,

1464
00:56:03,000 --> 00:56:04,767
they just might have a chance.

1465
00:56:04,767 --> 00:56:05,667
- A chance?

1466
00:56:05,667 --> 00:56:06,500
- Yes.

1467
00:56:07,367 --> 00:56:09,633
They are the only hope we have.

1468
00:56:09,633 --> 00:56:11,533
- [Joel] Please cross
behind the actors.

1469
00:56:11,533 --> 00:56:12,533
Do you mind?

1470
00:56:13,600 --> 00:56:14,800
- Well, that settles it.

1471
00:56:14,800 --> 00:56:16,200
Let's go to dance class.

1472
00:56:17,467 --> 00:56:19,567
- [Servo] And Ramses
said to build a city.

1473
00:56:22,200 --> 00:56:23,500
- My favorite food?

1474
00:56:23,500 --> 00:56:25,167
Cherry Pez, no
question about it.

1475
00:56:27,533 --> 00:56:28,800
- Why should we
wait out the night?

1476
00:56:28,800 --> 00:56:30,667
We should strike now.

1477
00:56:30,667 --> 00:56:33,567
- The morning will
be soon enough.

1478
00:56:33,567 --> 00:56:37,467
- [Klyton] The power station
cannot track us by night.

1479
00:56:37,467 --> 00:56:40,700
- All the more reason we
should attack them now.

1480
00:56:40,700 --> 00:56:42,133
- Sleep.

1481
00:56:42,133 --> 00:56:45,333
They don't know if we
are even still alive.

1482
00:56:45,333 --> 00:56:46,533
- He's right.

1483
00:56:46,533 --> 00:56:48,700
- [Joel] You know we
could make some s'mores.

1484
00:56:48,700 --> 00:56:50,333
- No because he's right.

1485
00:56:50,333 --> 00:56:52,200
Besides if we sleep
now for a few hours

1486
00:56:52,200 --> 00:56:53,667
we'll be that much alert

1487
00:56:53,667 --> 00:56:54,733
for what lies ahead
in the morning.

1488
00:56:54,733 --> 00:56:55,933
- You're hopeless.

1489
00:56:55,933 --> 00:56:57,100
A man tells you what to do

1490
00:56:57,100 --> 00:56:59,000
and you follow his
orders without question.

1491
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:00,900
- I'm following nobody's order.

1492
00:57:00,900 --> 00:57:02,867
Neo just makes the most sense.

1493
00:57:02,867 --> 00:57:04,133
- Suit yourself.

1494
00:57:04,133 --> 00:57:05,233
We wake up dead in the morning,

1495
00:57:05,233 --> 00:57:06,367
you know who's to blame.

1496
00:57:06,367 --> 00:57:07,333
- [Servo] Funny, we'll be dead.

1497
00:57:07,333 --> 00:57:08,400
What a spaz.

1498
00:57:11,600 --> 00:57:13,000
- [Joel] There's the Nudge.

1499
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:15,633
Locked, cocked, ready to rock.

1500
00:57:16,533 --> 00:57:17,667
- Dude.
- Dog scratch,

1501
00:57:17,667 --> 00:57:18,600
No, no, no.

1502
00:57:18,600 --> 00:57:19,700
Cat, cat scratch.

1503
00:57:19,700 --> 00:57:20,900
I gotta tell somebody.

1504
00:57:20,900 --> 00:57:22,400
Cat scratch fever,
this is great.

1505
00:57:22,400 --> 00:57:25,233
(low tense music)

1506
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:30,533
- What is it little fella?

1507
00:57:30,533 --> 00:57:31,900
Snack, you gotta go walkies?

1508
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:37,933
- [Servo] I can't believe
she's sleeping with an android.

1509
00:57:37,933 --> 00:57:39,533
- Ow.
- Gone.

1510
00:57:39,533 --> 00:57:41,267
And his brother
called me a coward.

1511
00:57:43,600 --> 00:57:46,800
- He's gone on ahead.

1512
00:57:46,800 --> 00:57:47,633
- How long ago?

1513
00:57:47,633 --> 00:57:48,667
Can you tell?

1514
00:57:48,667 --> 00:57:50,167
- No.

1515
00:57:50,167 --> 00:57:53,800
- [Klyton] He is headed
towards the power station.

1516
00:57:53,800 --> 00:57:55,700
- Come, we must follow.

1517
00:57:55,700 --> 00:57:58,200
(tense music)

1518
00:58:02,633 --> 00:58:05,067
- Have you freed the
surveillance drone?

1519
00:58:05,067 --> 00:58:06,400
- Yes, mistress.

1520
00:58:07,600 --> 00:58:10,700
It has been caged
for sometime now.

1521
00:58:10,700 --> 00:58:13,133
So, it should be very hungry.

1522
00:58:14,200 --> 00:58:15,800
- Go into the tunnels
and prepare...

1523
00:58:15,800 --> 00:58:16,733
- [Joel] Do you think they shop

1524
00:58:16,733 --> 00:58:18,800
at the same place Mad Max does?

1525
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:21,100
- I don't want it
attacking the girl.

1526
00:58:21,100 --> 00:58:23,233
She must get here alive.

1527
00:58:23,233 --> 00:58:24,400
- Yes, mistress.

1528
00:58:25,633 --> 00:58:28,167
- [Servo] I love it when
he calls me mistress.

1529
00:58:33,567 --> 00:58:35,800
- Hey, I had a dream about
a big donut like that.

1530
00:58:35,800 --> 00:58:37,367
- [Servo] You know
what that means.

1531
00:58:37,367 --> 00:58:38,500
- [Joel] He was hungry?

1532
00:58:41,467 --> 00:58:43,333
- [Servo] Sometimes a
donut is just a donut.

1533
00:58:43,333 --> 00:58:44,967
