1787
01:09:58,000 --> 01:09:59,400
- [Servo] Nuh uh.

1788
01:10:00,600 --> 01:10:03,333
- From where I stand, I
can't see what you can.

1789
01:10:03,333 --> 01:10:06,100
There should be a steel
cylinder in front of you,

1790
01:10:06,100 --> 01:10:07,467
near your head.

1791
01:10:07,467 --> 01:10:09,000
Is there?

1792
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:11,100
- If that thing goes off,
he'll be playing Vincent.

1793
01:10:11,100 --> 01:10:13,467
- Is there a small nod
at the tip of one end?

1794
01:10:15,300 --> 01:10:16,567
- [Servo] No knob.

1795
01:10:16,567 --> 01:10:20,000
- Slowly, move your
hand up to the bomb

1796
01:10:20,000 --> 01:10:22,300
without touching the
wires at your side.

1797
01:10:25,467 --> 01:10:27,833
- [Joel] But before you do that.

1798
01:10:27,833 --> 01:10:30,333
(tense music)

1799
01:10:32,033 --> 01:10:33,533
- Have you got it?

1800
01:10:35,000 --> 01:10:37,400
- Now, reach into your
left breast pocket.

1801
01:10:37,400 --> 01:10:40,067
- The knob is a
trigger mechanism.

1802
01:10:40,067 --> 01:10:42,200
It is attached to the
explosives on the inside

1803
01:10:42,200 --> 01:10:43,800
by a very short wire.

1804
01:10:45,567 --> 01:10:48,467
Klyton, do you have
cutters in your tool panel?

1805
01:10:48,467 --> 01:10:50,700
- [Servo] Well that's a
little personal, isn't it?

1806
01:10:50,700 --> 01:10:53,167
(tense music)

1807
01:10:56,767 --> 01:10:58,367
- [Joel] Are martinis
good for you guys?

1808
01:10:58,367 --> 01:11:00,200
Everybody interested.

1809
01:11:00,200 --> 01:11:02,333
- Carefully unscrew the
knob on the cylinder.

1810
01:11:04,100 --> 01:11:06,433
When it's loose,
don't pull it away.

1811
01:11:06,433 --> 01:11:07,700
Do you understand?

1812
01:11:07,700 --> 01:11:09,100
- [Joel] And don't breathe.

1813
01:11:09,100 --> 01:11:09,933
- Is it loose?

1814
01:11:12,533 --> 01:11:15,633
I'm reaching behind
you with the cutters.

1815
01:11:15,633 --> 01:11:16,900
- [Servo] When I'm
done with this,

1816
01:11:16,900 --> 01:11:19,200
you will guard my
harem, understand?

1817
01:11:20,700 --> 01:11:23,200
(tense music)

1818
01:11:28,833 --> 01:11:30,100
- And don't clip your nails.

1819
01:11:30,100 --> 01:11:31,300
- Are the cutters
near the cylinder?

1820
01:11:33,633 --> 01:11:34,467
Cut it.

1821
01:11:35,400 --> 01:11:36,200
Slowly.

1822
01:11:37,400 --> 01:11:40,700
Pull the knob away
from the cylinder

1823
01:11:40,700 --> 01:11:44,200
just enough to put the
cutters between the knob

1824
01:11:44,200 --> 01:11:45,467
and the head of the bomb.

1825
01:11:50,000 --> 01:11:51,100
Cut the wire.

1826
01:11:52,367 --> 01:11:53,167
Now.

1827
01:11:56,467 --> 01:11:57,267
- Poink.

1828
01:11:59,867 --> 01:12:01,900
- [Joel] Uh, I
haven't cut it yet.

1829
01:12:01,900 --> 01:12:02,733
Just kidding.

1830
01:12:03,800 --> 01:12:07,333
Just fake you're
cutting the wires still.

1831
01:12:07,333 --> 01:12:09,100
- Larry, our pizzas here.

1832
01:12:09,100 --> 01:12:10,233
- What is it?

1833
01:12:10,233 --> 01:12:11,833
- [Torque] The energy reservoir.

1834
01:12:11,833 --> 01:12:13,067
- Deep dish.

1835
01:12:13,067 --> 01:12:14,267
- [Torque] From
the amphitheater.

1836
01:12:14,267 --> 01:12:15,267
- [Servo] That guy needs
a Kleenex real bad.

1837
01:12:15,267 --> 01:12:17,033
- But we saw them working.

1838
01:12:17,033 --> 01:12:19,133
- [Dark One] What
did see, Valaria?

1839
01:12:19,133 --> 01:12:21,000
- The Airslaves, they--

1840
01:12:21,000 --> 01:12:22,967
- [Dark One] Airslaves?

1841
01:12:22,967 --> 01:12:23,900
- [Servo] What?

1842
01:12:23,900 --> 01:12:25,100
- [Dark One] The beast of burden

1843
01:12:25,100 --> 01:12:27,267
and they somehow
got the best of you.

1844
01:12:27,267 --> 01:12:29,933
Valaria, what am
I to do with you?

1845
01:12:29,933 --> 01:12:31,433
- Dark One, please.

1846
01:12:31,433 --> 01:12:33,733
- [Dark One] Torque, take
her away from my sight.

1847
01:12:33,733 --> 01:12:35,233
- No, Dark One, please.

1848
01:12:35,233 --> 01:12:37,400
- [Joel] Taking someone out of
an omnipresent being's sight

1849
01:12:37,400 --> 01:12:40,333
is pretty tough to do
when you think about it.

1850
01:12:40,333 --> 01:12:42,133
- [Servo] But don't.

1851
01:12:42,133 --> 01:12:44,200
- I will bring the
girl to you myself

1852
01:12:44,200 --> 01:12:46,700
and she will tell you
what you want to know.

1853
01:12:46,700 --> 01:12:47,900
(Servo clearing throat)

1854
01:12:47,900 --> 01:12:49,233
- [Dark One] One
last chance, Valaria

1855
01:12:49,233 --> 01:12:52,500
and then you'll know the
fate that awaits you.

1856
01:12:52,500 --> 01:12:53,733
- Thank, you Dark One.

1857
01:12:53,733 --> 01:12:54,567
- Diction school.

1858
01:12:54,567 --> 01:12:57,033
(tense music)

1859
01:12:59,100 --> 01:13:00,867
- [Joel] Oh,
pulsating glass ball

1860
01:13:00,867 --> 01:13:02,800
with hair like Sam Donaldson.

1861
01:13:02,800 --> 01:13:04,733
Please tell me what to do.

1862
01:13:04,733 --> 01:13:06,767
We better get out of here.

1863
01:13:06,767 --> 01:13:07,833
- [Crow] Carry me?

1864
01:13:07,833 --> 01:13:09,900
- [Joel] No.

1865
01:13:09,900 --> 01:13:11,733
- Torque, summon the guardbots.

1866
01:13:13,600 --> 01:13:16,367
(doors whirring)

1867
01:13:23,633 --> 01:13:25,200
- It was after the apocalypse.

1868
01:13:25,200 --> 01:13:27,667
It was after the robots
had taken over the Earth.

1869
01:13:27,667 --> 01:13:29,533
There stood a lone,
desperate survivor

1870
01:13:29,533 --> 01:13:31,267
in a dark dangerous time.

1871
01:13:31,267 --> 01:13:32,600
Crow the hunter

1872
01:13:32,600 --> 01:13:34,567
and his animal boy, Geekor.

1873
01:13:34,567 --> 01:13:36,400
A lowly human
dressed in the skins

1874
01:13:36,400 --> 01:13:38,067
of those lesser
on the food chain

1875
01:13:38,067 --> 01:13:39,533
but not by much.

1876
01:13:39,533 --> 01:13:42,667
The boldest of them all
was Servo the Blood letter.

1877
01:13:42,667 --> 01:13:45,067
Servo the chirping hell beast.

1878
01:13:45,067 --> 01:13:47,367
Servo, the defiler
of all that is...

1879
01:13:48,300 --> 01:13:49,667
Oh yeah, okay.

1880
01:13:49,667 --> 01:13:51,767
So the lonely
triumvirate strode forth

1881
01:13:51,767 --> 01:13:53,533
in a search for the morphotic
terror awaiting them

1882
01:13:53,533 --> 01:13:55,733
in the dark, evil
power quadrant.

1883
01:13:55,733 --> 01:13:58,500
- Uh hey, can we stop at
a Wendy's first, guys?

1884
01:13:58,500 --> 01:14:00,933
Geekor here wants a
frosty in a bad way.

1885
01:14:00,933 --> 01:14:02,567
- Silence, beaked fool.

1886
01:14:02,567 --> 01:14:05,333
You are to mock the
power of the dog wan?

1887
01:14:05,333 --> 01:14:07,000
- The blocked wand?

1888
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:07,833
- Bog wan?

1889
01:14:07,833 --> 01:14:08,767
What?

1890
01:14:08,767 --> 01:14:10,200
- The Dark One, the Dark One.

1891
01:14:10,200 --> 01:14:12,200
- Oh, Dark One.

1892
01:14:12,200 --> 01:14:13,600
Listen, you know Tom Servo,

1893
01:14:13,600 --> 01:14:14,833
I'm not getting too into this.

1894
01:14:14,833 --> 01:14:16,467
I feel kinda like King Vitamin

1895
01:14:16,467 --> 01:14:18,933
miscast in a Sonny
and Cher video

1896
01:14:18,933 --> 01:14:21,000
and besides, are these
real furs or what?

1897
01:14:21,000 --> 01:14:23,100
- Yeah, what are we
wearing, roadkill here?

1898
01:14:23,100 --> 01:14:25,967
I mean, hey these, these furs

1899
01:14:25,967 --> 01:14:27,633
are either cruel or unsanitary,

1900
01:14:27,633 --> 01:14:29,100
depending on your point of view.

1901
01:14:29,100 --> 01:14:32,467
- Well, it's after the
apocalypse and everything

1902
01:14:32,467 --> 01:14:34,033
and well we got the furs

1903
01:14:34,033 --> 01:14:36,567
from the dead animals
littering the countryside.

1904
01:14:36,567 --> 01:14:37,600
- Ah, roadkill.

1905
01:14:37,600 --> 01:14:38,667
See, I told ya, Joel.

1906
01:14:38,667 --> 01:14:39,800
We're wearing roadkill.

1907
01:14:39,800 --> 01:14:40,800
- Well, that's just great.

1908
01:14:40,800 --> 01:14:42,567
Tom Servo is having some kind

1909
01:14:42,567 --> 01:14:46,033
of rightwing
conservative fur party

1910
01:14:46,033 --> 01:14:48,500
and I think we should
just leave him, Crow.

1911
01:14:48,500 --> 01:14:51,033
Let's left mister
narcissist alone here

1912
01:14:51,033 --> 01:14:53,800
so he can have his
own party of access.

1913
01:14:53,800 --> 01:14:55,067
Let's get out of here.

1914
01:14:55,067 --> 01:14:57,000
- Yeah, see ya at the
seal clubbing meeting.

1915
01:14:57,000 --> 01:14:57,833
Not.

1916
01:15:01,367 --> 01:15:02,767
- He stood proudly.

1917
01:15:03,967 --> 01:15:07,067
The bold survivor of the
weak and unwilling race.

1918
01:15:08,167 --> 01:15:09,833
You're all my
friends, aren't you?

1919
01:15:09,833 --> 01:15:11,133
Tell me your deep dark secrets,

1920
01:15:11,133 --> 01:15:12,233
my little furry friends.

1921
01:15:12,233 --> 01:15:13,400
We'll roam the countryside

1922
01:15:13,400 --> 01:15:15,200
and we'll be one together.

1923
01:15:16,133 --> 01:15:18,700
(upbeat music)

1924
01:15:22,133 --> 01:15:24,633
(tense music)

1925
01:15:27,167 --> 01:15:28,900
- [Joel] Okay, now
I don't want you--

1926
01:15:28,900 --> 01:15:30,433
- [Servo] We shall
rule the planet.

1927
01:15:30,433 --> 01:15:32,000
- [Joel] I don't want you
wearing this hat anymore.

1928
01:15:32,000 --> 01:15:32,967
- [Servo] Hey.

1929
01:15:32,967 --> 01:15:34,567
- Hey, that guy had a tough day.

1930
01:15:34,567 --> 01:15:36,400
He's off the Murray's
for a Schmidty.

1931
01:15:41,467 --> 01:15:42,400
- [Servo] Ever see this one?

1932
01:15:42,400 --> 01:15:43,833
We can walk the dog, too.

1933
01:15:47,967 --> 01:15:50,700
(metal clanging)

1934
01:16:06,500 --> 01:16:08,833
- Boy, if I could fight
like those robots.

1935
01:16:08,833 --> 01:16:09,800
Boy, this is what I'd do.

1936
01:16:09,800 --> 01:16:11,300
I'd get me some swords

1937
01:16:11,300 --> 01:16:13,900
and they wouldn't stand
a chance against me.

1938
01:16:16,367 --> 01:16:18,400
- [Joel] Now, how much would
you pay for this robot?

1939
01:16:18,400 --> 01:16:19,433
Wait, stop.

1940
01:16:19,433 --> 01:16:20,333
There's more.

1941
01:16:20,333 --> 01:16:22,200
It slices, it dices.

1942
01:16:22,200 --> 01:16:24,400
It makes a great julienne fry.

1943
01:16:24,400 --> 01:16:26,167
- [Servo] Hey, not
bad for a crustacean.

1944
01:16:26,167 --> 01:16:27,400
Sure, I got my pan flute.

1945
01:16:27,400 --> 01:16:29,500
Maybe I should of
brought an oyster knife.

1946
01:16:35,833 --> 01:16:37,167
- [Klyton] Let me get.

1947
01:16:37,167 --> 01:16:38,000
How did I?

1948
01:16:39,067 --> 01:16:40,567
Oh.

1949
01:16:40,567 --> 01:16:43,233
- In the future, all robots
will act like Don Knotts.

1950
01:16:44,833 --> 01:16:45,867
- [Servo] Hey.

1951
01:16:45,867 --> 01:16:47,300
- [Klyton] Oh no.

1952
01:16:52,333 --> 01:16:54,367
- [Joel] I saw Darth
Vader do that once.

1953
01:16:55,667 --> 01:16:57,300
Uh, uh, you got it.

1954
01:17:02,233 --> 01:17:03,233
- [Servo] Cat fight.

1955
01:17:11,000 --> 01:17:12,433
- [Joel] Right in the throat.

1956
01:17:14,333 --> 01:17:16,633
- See, Dark One,
I kept my promise.

1957
01:17:16,633 --> 01:17:18,267
The girl is your.

1958
01:17:18,267 --> 01:17:20,267
- [Dark One] You are as
good as your word, Valaria

1959
01:17:20,267 --> 01:17:23,700
but your use to me has
still come to an end.

1960
01:17:23,700 --> 01:17:26,500
- But, Dark One, I
delivered on my promise.

1961
01:17:26,500 --> 01:17:29,133
- [Dark One] Life isn't
always fair, Valaria.

1962
01:17:29,133 --> 01:17:30,300
Especially...

1963
01:17:30,300 --> 01:17:31,800
- [Joel] Oh, always
get a contract

1964
01:17:31,800 --> 01:17:34,167
when you're dealing with
a dark, omnipotent power.

1965
01:17:35,267 --> 01:17:36,167
You gotta do that.

1966
01:17:39,767 --> 01:17:41,633
- Joel, if we ever
get like these bots,

1967
01:17:41,633 --> 01:17:43,367
will you please shut us down?

1968
01:17:43,367 --> 01:17:44,867
- [Servo] Just take us out.

1969
01:17:47,700 --> 01:17:49,900
- [Joel] She shouldn't be
by that Worthington machine.

1970
01:17:49,900 --> 01:17:51,867
You know, those things are known

1971
01:17:51,867 --> 01:17:54,267
to have a problem
with their, uh, yeah.

1972
01:17:55,600 --> 01:17:56,900
- [Servo] She wasn't
wearing her safety goggles.

1973
01:17:56,900 --> 01:17:57,867
- [Joel] That's a problem.

1974
01:17:57,867 --> 01:17:59,267
- [Servo] Should of expected it.

1975
01:17:59,267 --> 01:18:01,600
(screaming)

1976
01:18:03,033 --> 01:18:03,967
- She likes it.

1977
01:18:03,967 --> 01:18:05,467
- Dark One, can you hear me?

1978
01:18:05,467 --> 01:18:07,433
- [Dark One] Yes, Valaria,
what do you wish to say

1979
01:18:07,433 --> 01:18:09,333
before you die?

1980
01:18:09,333 --> 01:18:10,600
- You were the one who said it,

1981
01:18:10,600 --> 01:18:12,333
I was never really alive.

1982
01:18:12,333 --> 01:18:17,333
So what matters to me what
becomes of your followers.

1983
01:18:18,733 --> 01:18:20,567
- [Joel] She sounds kinda
like an Obsession commercial.

1984
01:18:20,567 --> 01:18:23,633
- The self destruction lever.

1985
01:18:23,633 --> 01:18:24,667
- [Servo] Hey
don't turn that up.

1986
01:18:24,667 --> 01:18:27,400
Power company says 68, tops.

1987
01:18:27,400 --> 01:18:28,333
- The fries are up.

1988
01:18:31,633 --> 01:18:33,100
- In five minutes, all of
your domain will be destroyed.

1989
01:18:36,000 --> 01:18:36,933
- [Servo] That blast to her face

1990
01:18:36,933 --> 01:18:38,700
kinda helped her diction.

1991
01:18:38,700 --> 01:18:40,433
- And you and all the others

1992
01:18:40,433 --> 01:18:42,367
will cease to exist.

1993
01:18:42,367 --> 01:18:45,567
- Well, good as long as
we don't cease to exist.

1994
01:18:46,567 --> 01:18:47,567
- Or what?

1995
01:18:47,567 --> 01:18:49,267
You will destroy me?

1996
01:18:49,267 --> 01:18:51,200
It doesn't matter anymore.

1997
01:18:51,200 --> 01:18:52,267
Nothing does.

1998
01:18:53,533 --> 01:18:55,067
- [Joel] I don't know
what's gotten into her.

1999
01:18:55,067 --> 01:18:57,633
She just doesn't sound like
the malaria I used to know.

2000
01:18:59,133 --> 01:19:01,133
- [Servo] Wow, he's, whoa.

2001
01:19:01,133 --> 01:19:02,933
- [Joel] Oh, it's the huge Nuge.

2002
01:19:02,933 --> 01:19:05,667
(dramatic music)

2003
01:19:08,800 --> 01:19:10,267
- That's for R2-D2.

2004
01:19:10,267 --> 01:19:12,067
That's for C-3PO.

2005
01:19:12,067 --> 01:19:14,167
That's for Julie Newmar

2006
01:19:14,167 --> 01:19:16,333
and that's just 'cause I wanna.

2007
01:19:16,333 --> 01:19:17,333
What have I done?

2008
01:19:18,200 --> 01:19:19,633
- [Joel] Oh man, the huge Nuge.

2009
01:19:19,633 --> 01:19:22,167
He's got cat scratch
fever right on his chest.

2010
01:19:28,133 --> 01:19:30,267
- [Klyton] No, no!

2011
01:19:30,267 --> 01:19:31,667
- Would somebody get
those fries, please?

2012
01:19:31,667 --> 01:19:32,767
- Where is my father?

2013
01:19:32,767 --> 01:19:33,600
- [Servo] Which father?

2014
01:19:33,600 --> 01:19:34,533
That could be anyone.

2015
01:19:34,533 --> 01:19:35,300
- [Dark One] He is nearby.

2016
01:19:37,033 --> 01:19:37,867
- Take me to him.

2017
01:19:39,067 --> 01:19:40,967
- [Dark One] Tell me
what I want to know.

2018
01:19:40,967 --> 01:19:42,567
- [Joel] Okay, well
you're kinda cute,

2019
01:19:42,567 --> 01:19:43,467
you're kinda pretty,

2020
01:19:43,467 --> 01:19:44,400
you drive a big car, too

2021
01:19:44,400 --> 01:19:45,600
and when I hold you in my arms,

2022
01:19:45,600 --> 01:19:46,533
I never know what to do.

2023
01:19:46,533 --> 01:19:48,033
- [Dark One] You and your father

2024
01:19:48,033 --> 01:19:49,533
are immune to my powers.

2025
01:19:49,533 --> 01:19:50,567
Why?

2026
01:19:50,567 --> 01:19:52,167
- I don't know.

2027
01:19:52,167 --> 01:19:56,500
- [Dark One] You do and
you will tell me now.

2028
01:19:57,900 --> 01:19:59,867
- [Joel] You know, I kinda
miss Earth, you guys.

2029
01:20:01,200 --> 01:20:02,700
- [Servo] I can see why.

2030
01:20:02,700 --> 01:20:04,633
- Yeah, all that equipment.

2031
01:20:04,633 --> 01:20:06,033
- [Joel] Yeah, it's neat.

2032
01:20:12,567 --> 01:20:13,800
- Go ahead.

2033
01:20:13,800 --> 01:20:15,500
Waste your stupid
energies on each other.

2034
01:20:15,500 --> 01:20:17,567
- It's Eartha Kitt.

2035
01:20:17,567 --> 01:20:18,800
- What will it matter

2036
01:20:18,800 --> 01:20:21,867
in less than a minute
the entire power station

2037
01:20:21,867 --> 01:20:23,367
will be destroyed.

2038
01:20:27,667 --> 01:20:29,533
- [Torque] What have you done?

2039
01:20:29,533 --> 01:20:31,400
- [Joel] What hasn't she done?

2040
01:20:31,400 --> 01:20:32,467
